---
source: crates/zeff-ir/tests/instruments.rs
expression: all
---
== missing_from_the_formula
error[Z0504]: `educ` is instrumented but is not a regressor
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:40
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper, instruments: educ ~ nearc4)
  |                                        ^^^^ instrumented here, missing from the formula
  |
  = help: add it to the regressors: `lwage ~ exper + educ`


== one_of_two_missing
error[Z0504]: `tenure` is instrumented but is not a regressor
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:54
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: educ + tenure ~ nearc4 + nearc2)
  |                                                      ^^^^^^ instrumented here, missing from the formula
  |
  = help: add it to the regressors: `lwage ~ exper + educ + tenure`


== on_both_sides
error[Z0505]: `educ` is on both sides of `~` in `instruments:`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:63
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: educ ~ nearc4 + educ)
  |                                                               ^^^^ an instrument for itself
  |
  = help: the left of `~` holds the regressors that are instrumented and the right the variables that instrument them; `educ` belongs on one side


== under_identified
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: 1 excluded instrument for 2 instrumented regressors
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:47
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: educ + exper ~ nearc4)
  |                                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ fewer instruments than instrumented regressors
  |
  = help: each instrumented regressor needs at least one instrument that is not a regressor of the formula


== under_identified_once_an_instrument_is_included
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: 0 excluded instruments for 1 instrumented regressor
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:47
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: educ ~ exper)
  |                                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^ fewer instruments than instrumented regressors
  |
  = help: each instrumented regressor needs at least one instrument that is not a regressor of the formula
  = help: `exper` is already in the formula, so it is an included instrument and identifies nothing


== the_outcome_as_an_instrument
error[Z0401]: `lwage` is the outcome of the formula and cannot be an instrument
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:54
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: educ ~ lwage)
  |                                                      ^^^^^ the outcome
  |
  = help: `instruments:` names regressors of the formula on the left of `~` and variables outside it on the right; the outcome is neither


== the_outcome_instrumented
error[Z0401]: `lwage` is the outcome of the formula and cannot be instrumented
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:47
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: lwage ~ nearc4)
  |                                               ^^^^^ the outcome
  |
  = help: `instruments:` names regressors of the formula on the left of `~` and variables outside it on the right; the outcome is neither


== no_tilde
error[Z0401]: `instruments:` takes the instrumented regressors, `~`, and their instruments, and this has no `~`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:47
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: nearc4)
  |                                               ^^^^^^ not `endog ~ instr`
  |
  = help: write `instruments: educ ~ nearc4`; several of either are joined with `+`: `instruments: educ + exper ~ nearc4 + nearc2 + age2`


== nothing_on_the_left
error[Z0401]: `instruments:` takes the instrumented regressors, `~`, and their instruments, and nothing stands on the left of `~`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:47
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: ~ nearc4)
  |                                               ^^^^^^^^ no instrumented regressor
  |
  = help: write `instruments: educ ~ nearc4`; several of either are joined with `+`: `instruments: educ + exper ~ nearc4 + nearc2 + age2`


== a_term_removed
error[Z0401]: `instruments:` takes the instrumented regressors, `~`, and their instruments, and `- nearc2` removes nothing from them
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:63
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: educ ~ nearc4 - nearc2)
  |                                                               ^^^^^^ a term removed
  |
  = help: write `instruments: educ ~ nearc4`; several of either are joined with `+`: `instruments: educ + exper ~ nearc4 + nearc2 + age2`


== an_intercept
error[Z0401]: `instruments:` takes the instrumented regressors, `~`, and their instruments, and `1` is neither: the intercept is its own instrument
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:47
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: educ ~ nearc4 + 1)
  |                                               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ an intercept
  |
  = help: write `instruments: educ ~ nearc4`; several of either are joined with `+`: `instruments: educ + exper ~ nearc4 + nearc2 + age2`


== a_product_instrumented
error[Z0401]: `instruments:` takes the instrumented regressors, `~`, and their instruments, and `educ * black` is several terms at once
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:55
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ * black, instruments: educ * black ~ nearc4)
  |                                                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^ name each instrumented term: `a + b + a:b`
  |
  = help: write `instruments: educ ~ nearc4`; several of either are joined with `+`: `instruments: educ + exper ~ nearc4 + nearc2 + age2`


== a_text
error[Z0401]: `instruments:` takes the instrumented regressors, `~`, and their instruments, and this has no `~`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:47
  |
2 | card.ivreg(lwage ~ exper + educ, instruments: "nearc4")
  |                                               ^^^^^^^^ not `endog ~ instr`
  |
  = help: write `instruments: educ ~ nearc4`; several of either are joined with `+`: `instruments: educ + exper ~ nearc4 + nearc2 + age2`
